# Local secrets for `docker compose --env-file deploy/local.env up`. Copy to deploy/local.env
# (gitignored, must stay untracked) and fill in — plain `KEY=value`, not YAML: docker's env-file
# parser reads `KEY: "value"` as a literal key named `KEY` and the value is never applied.
#
# This is the *development* shape. Outside local compose, prefer file-backed secrets: set
# TANKOVAULT_SECRETS_DIR to a directory holding one file per key (`auth__jwt_secret`, …), or
# point TANKOVAULT_<KEY>_FILE at a single path. Both keep the value out of the process
# environment and let it be rotated without a restart — docs/CONFIGURATION.md §7. Setting a key
# here *and* in a file is refused at boot, so migrate a key rather than duplicating it.

# Internal service-to-service identity (required in production). One credential per *caller*,
# not one per tier: each service accepts only the callers its route table names, so a leaked
# token opens the routes that one caller may reach and nothing else.
#
# `api` calls control-plane, sync and worker. `worker` calls challenge-solver and render.
# Nothing else calls anything, so these two are the whole set. Generate each separately —
# reusing one value for both rebuilds the tier-wide secret this replaced.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
TANKOVAULT_INTERNAL_TOKEN_API=
TANKOVAULT_INTERNAL_TOKEN_WORKER=

# Auth. At least 32 bytes; the known dev placeholder is rejected at boot in every profile.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
TANKOVAULT_AUTH__JWT_SECRET=
# Server-side pepper mixed into every argon2id hash. Rotating it invalidates all passwords.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
TANKOVAULT_AUTH__PASSWORD_PEPPER=
# Initial administrator password for the one-shot `seed` step. Change on first sign-in.
TANKOVAULT_SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# AniList OAuth (external sync). Register an application at
# https://anilist.co/settings/developer and paste its values.
TANKOVAULT_ANILIST__CLIENT_ID=
TANKOVAULT_ANILIST__CLIENT_SECRET=
# Seals every user's AniList token at rest — losing it forces every account to re-link, leaking
# it exposes every stored token. Base64 32 bytes.
#   openssl rand -base64 32
TANKOVAULT_ANILIST__TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# Sentry (optional; unset ⇒ no client is installed and nothing leaves the process).
#
# The DSN is a credential for the project's ingest endpoint: outside compose, mount it through
# TANKOVAULT_SECRETS_DIR rather than putting it in the environment. Setting ENABLED=true with
# no DSN is refused at boot — a reporter that reports nowhere is the failure this refuses to
# repeat. TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE stays 0 until you want performance data; 0.1 is a normal
# production figure. See docs/CONFIGURATION.md §4 `telemetry.sentry`.
TANKOVAULT_SENTRY_ENABLED=false
TANKOVAULT_SENTRY_DSN=
TANKOVAULT_SENTRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE=0

# Transactional email (optional; unset ⇒ no-op mailer, those flows skip sending)
TANKOVAULT_EMAIL__HOST=
TANKOVAULT_EMAIL__PORT=587
TANKOVAULT_EMAIL__SECURITY=starttls
TANKOVAULT_EMAIL__USERNAME=
TANKOVAULT_EMAIL__PASSWORD=
TANKOVAULT_EMAIL__FROM=

# Legal documents (optional). The compose file mounts ./legal and points `dir` at it, so the
# checked-in samples work out of the box — they say "sample, not legal text" in their first line
# and must be replaced before anyone else uses the instance.
#
# The map is slug-keyed, so an operator can publish a document this build has never heard of
# (`dmca`, `acceptable_use`) without a code change. Address one leaf at a time with the usual
# `__` nesting:
#   TANKOVAULT_LEGAL__DOCUMENTS__IMPRINT__URL=https://example.org/impressum
#   TANKOVAULT_LEGAL__DOCUMENTS__TERMS__SOURCES__EN=/etc/tankovault/legal/terms.en.md
# A whole map spelled as JSON in one variable does **not** work: the environment layer is
# figment's `Env` provider split on `__`, so the JSON arrives as a string and the service exits
# with "expected a map for key LEGAL.DOCUMENTS". Point TANKOVAULT_CONFIG at a TOML file for a
# document set large enough that per-leaf variables stop being readable.
# A document with neither `sources` nor `url` — or with both — is refused at boot, naming the slug.
TANKOVAULT_LEGAL__DIR=
